  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "It is my collarbone, doctor. I broke my collarbone three months ago, fell off my scooter on a wet road. They said it has healed, but I am still having pain in the collarbone.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:32",
      "end_timestamp": "00:47",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "It is a dull ache mostly, right on top of the bone. Sometimes sharp, like a pinch, when I lift my arm up.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:58",
      "end_timestamp": "01:08",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Carrying my laptop bag on that shoulder. What to do, I have my files.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:21",
      "end_timestamp": "01:29",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "A hot water bag in the evening helps a little.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:39",
      "end_timestamp": "01:45",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Moderate, I would say. Not unbearable, but I notice it all day.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:53",
      "end_timestamp": "01:59",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "There is a stiffness in the shoulder, mostly in the morning. It loosens up after I move around.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:09",
      "end_timestamp": "02:17",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, there is a bump. A small bump right in the middle of the bone, which was not there earlier.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:26",
      "end_timestamp": "02:37",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'll have a look at that shortly. Have you had any numbness in your fingers on that side?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:38",
      "end_timestamp": "02:47",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, no numbness. I can type, I can hold my cup, all normal on that front.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:48",
      "end_timestamp": "02:57",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good. And any pain in the neck as well?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:00",
      "end_timestamp": "03:04",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, the neck is fine. It is only the collarbone area.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:06",
      "end_timestamp": "03:11",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That's very helpful. Now a few general questions. Any problems with breathing or a cough since the fall?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:14",
      "end_timestamp": "03:23",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, nothing like that.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:24",
      "end_timestamp": "03:26",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Just the thyroid. I have an underactive thyroid, since about five years.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:35",
      "end_timestamp": "03:41",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, thyroxine, 50 micrograms every morning, on an empty stomach. My wife reminds me.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:48",
      "end_timestamp": "03:54",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That's a clever reminder. And what work do you do?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:57",
      "end_timestamp": "04:02",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I am an accountant, in a firm near the station. Desk work mostly, with lots of files going between offices.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:03",
      "end_timestamp": "04:14",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That explains the bag. Do you smoke at all?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:15",
      "end_timestamp": "04:20",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, no, I have never smoked.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:22",
      "end_timestamp": "04:25",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "No problem at all. I can feel a firm, bony bump over the middle of the collarbone, and it's a little tender when I press.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:59",
      "end_timestamp": "05:11",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Let me finish looking. There's no redness and no warmth, so no sign of infection. Now lift your arm up slowly for me.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:29",
      "end_timestamp": "05:40",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "This is the usual thing. When a collarbone heals, the body lays down extra bone around the break, like a patch on a tyre. This looks like a healing callus, and the ache is the bone settling down.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:10",
      "end_timestamp": "06:26",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Simple ones. Slowly circle the shoulder, then reach the arm forward and up as far as is comfortable. Ten times, morning and evening, no forcing.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:35",
      "end_timestamp": "07:47",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Switch to a rucksack with two straps so the weight is shared, and give the shoulder a rest from heavy loads for a while.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:57",
      "end_timestamp": "08:09",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    }
